hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27668","Haddathana Ya'la ibn Ubayd, he said: Haddathana al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, from Umm Tariq, freedwoman of Sa'd, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Sa'd and asked permission, and Sa'd was silent, then he repeated and Sa'd was silent, then he repeated and Sa'd was silent, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left. She said: Then Sa'd sent me to him: Nothing prevented us from permitting you except that we wanted you to add more. She said: Then I heard a voice at the door asking permission, but I saw nothing, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who are you? She said: Umm Mildam. He said: No welcome to you and no greeting; do you gift yourself to the people of Quba? She said: Yes. He said: Then go to them."
